# Vale Totems: offerings that arrive with a world hop (the game sending your sites' counts again)
# are not offerings an ent left while you played. Only the rise seen after the hop counts towards
# the next totem kept, and that totem is timed from your return.
#
# Facts: the site varbits as the Totem Fletching plugin by TheRealGuru reads them (a cross-check);
# OSRS wiki, Vale Totems: "Every 80 ticks (48 seconds), Ents travel between these sites, leaving
# offerings at completed totems"
include /replays/scenes/totems.scene
skill HITPOINTS 10
skill FLETCHING 60
items INV set KNIFE 1 UNSTRUNG_MAPLE_SHORTBOW 1
varbit ENT_TOTEMS_SITE_1_BASE 3
varbit ENT_TOTEMS_SITE_1_BASE_CARVED 1
varbit ENT_TOTEMS_SITE_1_DECORATIONS 3
at 1381 3321
tick
expect step = "Decorate the totem (3 of 4)"
# An ent at site 2's finished totem leaves 200 offerings while you work.
varbit ENT_TOTEMS_SITE_2_POINTS 200
tick 2

# A hop: the counts come back higher than last seen, as they would after time away.
state HOPPING
varbit ENT_TOTEMS_SITE_2_POINTS 700
state LOGGED_IN
tick
varbit ENT_TOTEMS_SITE_2_POINTS 750
tick
xp FLETCHING 274742
varbit ENT_TOTEMS_SITE_1_DECORATIONS 4
tick
# 50 offerings seen after the hop, not the 200 before it nor the 500 the hop brought; 1,000 xp
# over the 2 ticks since you were back.
expect saved.totems.kept ~ ",2,MAPLE,1000,50"
